{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966788,"nonce":"EhLG48sE0xOdJMaSYPXHOTrDf7E=","title":"DSL match works in a widget body but mounts nothing directly under view {} with no container","message":"The Blinc DSL has had `match e { \"a\" -\u003e f(), _ -\u003e g() }` (string-literal and struct patterns, `_` wildcard) for a while, desugared by `lower_match_blocks` into an if-chain rather than using Zyntax's native `TypedStatement::Match`.\n\nInside a widget body the arms become that widget's children, which is the shape a navigation view wants:\n\n```\ncn.SidebarContent { with { Div { match page.get() { \"forms\" -\u003e FormWidgets(), _ -\u003e Home() } } } }\n```\n\n**Directly under `view { … }` with no container around it, a match still mounts nothing.** The arms run, but the arm block's value is not the widget handle, so the view function is never promoted to value-returning and `render_view` hands back nothing. Wrap the match in a container.\n\n**Why:** three separate shapes had to line up for the widget-body case, and the failure mode in all of them was silent — it compiled, ran, and rendered an empty body. Child collection carried only `If`/`While` (a match lowers to a `Block`); the child-push rewriter walked statements only (a match lowers to an *expression*-form if-chain); and an expression-form `if` in statement position emits no branches, so the chain is rebuilt in statement form once its pushes are in place. Both forms are needed: closures want the expression one (statement form skips both branches there), widget bodies the statement one.\n\n**How to apply:** when adding a DSL statement kind, check both `collect_children_into` and `rewrite_child_pushes_in_stmt` — see gotcha dsl statement walkers must handle while. A test that only asserts the program compiles will not catch a dropped arm; assert on rendered text.","files":null}]}